  "conclusion": "A locked screen hides nothing by itself: the front and the unfocused window keep rendering (~122 rAF/s, transitions, trusted input, screenshots) without any measure, and background tabs, occluded and minimized windows need the same measures as on an unlocked screen; focus emulation plus the lite screencast restores every state. chrome-shell still treats every tab as hidden while the screen is locked, because the display usually turns off next; that case is not measured."
